ary': 'Discovery: 2977978 results | Destruction: 0 results | Transfer: 72 results | Reality: 2977968 results', 'evidence_plane': {'role': 'VERIFICATION_SUPPORT', 'purpose': 'four-direction search attack around a serious candidate: discovery/destruction/transfer/reality directions feed collision, adjudication and the dossier', 'complementary_plane': {'role': 'DISCOVERY_SUPPORT', 'location': 'RETRIEVE -> MECHANISM_SPACE (the structured evidence consumed by the five transformation operators)', 'stamp': 'mechanism_space.structured_evidence.items[].retrieval_role'}, 'state_vocabulary_contract': 'SEARCH_FAILED / SEARCH_PARTIAL / UNRESOLVED / UNKNOWN stay exactly what they are on BOTH planes — no outage may become absence; per-source error/unavailable fields are preserved in sources_hit'}, 'adjacent_industries_derivation': {'value': ['process industry fluidics', 'aerospace fuel systems'], 'epistemic_class': 'MODEL_DERIVED', 'method': 'keyword map ADJACENT_INDUSTRY_MAP in adapters.py'}, 'sources_hit': []}, cemetery_check={'verdict': 'WARNING', 'hard_blocks': 0, 'warnings': 9, 'lessons_consulted': 160, 'full': {'verdict': 'WARNING', 'hard_blocks': [], 'warnings': [{'cemetery_entry': 'CE-007', 'territory': 'CV-T07', 'mechanism': 'M5 mechanical anti-trauma flexible neck', 'epistemic_class': 'STRONG_CONSTRAINT', 'lesson': 'Before optimizing a solution, VERIFY THE PROBLEM EXISTS at the physics level. The IVC filter analogy (cantilevered) does not apply to the eShunt (both-ends-anchored supported beam). A compliant tube deforms around a rigid object, not the other way around.', 'action_required': 'Explicit justification required to proceed despite this constraint'}, {'cemetery_entry': 'CE-009', 'territory': 'CV-T06', 'mechanism': 'Mechanical snare via catheter (R1)', 'epistemic_class': 'STRONG_CONSTRAINT', 'lesson': 'Changing retrieval ACTIVATION does NOT change retrieval PHYSICS. Any retrieval mechanism for a permanently implanted endovascular anchor faces the same ingrowth ceiling. The problem is not HOW you pull — it is that the anchor is DESIGNED to be ingrown.', 'action_required': 'Explicit justification required to proceed despite this constraint'}, {'cemetery_entry': 'CE-011', 'territory': 'CV-T06', 'mechanism': 'Magnetic actuated release (R4)', 'epistemic_class': 'STRONG_CONSTRAINT', 'lesson': 'Magnetic actuation is incompatible with neurosurgical implants that must coexist with brain MRI. The 1/r3 force decay makes deep-tissue magnetic actuation fundamentally insufficient. Any mechanism requiring external magnetic actuation for a deep endovascular implant faces both MRI safety and force-distance constraints.', 'action_required': 'Explicit justification required to proceed despite this constraint'}, {'cemetery_entry': 'CE-012', 'territory': 'CV-T05 (R2-C3 phenotype discovery, Round 56 series)', 'mechanism': 'R2-C3 predictor v1 — pressure-trajectory + phenotype classification for VSS failure-type prediction', 'epistemic_class': 'STRONG_CONSTRAINT', 'lesson': "FROZEN THEOREM (sharpened per CEO Round 56o): 'Existing information + existing transformation + existing control, merely recombined, is insufficient. A combination qualifies only if it produces a demonstrably new technical effect that survives prior art and non-obviousness attack. A world-class invention needs a genuinely new technical information source, transformation, or control capability. Do not build an AI layer on top of an already-claimed sensing/control architecture.' NOTE: This theorem does NOT create a universal 'new sensor required' rule. A novel combination of existing measurements CAN qualify if it produces a new, technically non-obvious effect. The theorem rejects TRIVIAL recombination, not all combinations.", 'action_required': 'Explicit justification required to proceed despite this constraint'}, {'cemetery_entry': 'CE-013', 'territory': 'CV-T05 (R2-C3 phenotype discovery, Round 56 orthogonal search)', 'mechanism': 'OSV-4: HRV/autonomic state as orthogonal predictor for R2-C3', 'epistemic_class': 'STRONG_CONSTRAINT', 'lesson': "A signal can be GENUINELY ORTHOGONAL to a specific measurement architecture (Hakim measures pressure, not HRV) and still be a DOWNSTREAM CONSEQUENCE of the same physiological variable (ICP → sympathetic → HRV). Orthogonality to one architecture does not imply independence from the underlying physiology. Before claiming a signal is 'new information,' test whether it is causally downstream of an already-measured variable. If A → B and A is measured, then B is a proxy for A, not new information — even if B is measured by a different sensor.", 'action_required': 'Explicit justification required to proceed despite this constraint'}, {'cemetery_entry': 'CE-014', 'territory': 'RES-4 adaptive VSS (Round 56q-56r)', 'mechanism': 'RES-4 broad: adaptive cerebrospinal venous stent with sensing + flow regulation', 'epistemic_class': 'STRONG_CONSTRAINT', 'lesson': "FROZEN THEOREM CE-014: 'No result for our formulation is not evidence that the capability is absent. Patent searches must generate terminology from patent claims + descriptions + CPC classes + inventor vocabulary + adjacent technologies, not just internally coined phrases. A query-fragile search produces false negatives.' The machine must be better at discovering what competitors actually claimed than it is at inventing elegant names for what we hope is new.", 'action_required': 'Explicit justification required to proceed despite this constraint'}, {'cemetery_entry': 'CE-016', 'territory': 'Stroke thrombectomy (Round 56w-58)', 'mechanism': 'Stroke: clot-vessel adhesion isolation + measurement + strategy selection (Layer A: force-decomposition estimator v1)', 'epistemic_class': 'STRONG_CONSTRAINT', 'lesson': 'FROZEN THEOREM CE-016 (sharpened per CEO Round 58): A proposed latent quantity survives only when (1) identifiability is demonstrated under an EXPLICIT observation/dynamics model with full rank/observability analysis (not naive unknown-count), AND (2) identifiability REMAINS under plausible model uncertainty (each ideal assumption relaxed toward realistic physics and re-tested). A single favorable rank calculation under a convenient model is INSUFFICIENT. A single unfavorable perturbation model is ALSO INSUFFICIENT to claim universal non-identifiability — it only kills the specific estimator tested under that specific perturbation model. The correct procedure: (a) define state, observables, inputs, noise, known/unknown params; (b) build measurement equations; (c) test rank of Jacobian wrt unknown params; (d) perform adversarial model-uncertainty test: relax each assumption toward realistic physics and re-test identifiability under the combined relaxed model; (e) only if BOTH the ideal-model rank AND the adversarial-model rank hold (or constructively fail) can a universal claim (measurable OR non-measurable) be recorded.', 'action_required': 'Explicit justification required to proceed despite this constraint'}, {'cemetery_entry': 'CE-017', 'territory': 'Cross-cutting (extracted from Stroke Round 58; applies to all latent-variable inventions)', 'mechanism': 'Structural identifiability under a convenient model is not enough — adversarial model-uncertainty and practical-operation survival are mandatory', 'epistemic_class': 'STRONG_CONSTRAINT', 'lesson': 'FROZEN THEOREM CE-017: A discovery engine earns trust when it attacks its own successful proof harder than its unsuccessful ideas. Structural identifiability under a convenient model is not enough. A candidate must survive adversarial model uncertainty AND practical operation (safety, timing, decision value, first-pass vs post-hoc). The burden is bidirectional: (a) the proposer must demonstrate identifiability survives realistic model relaxation; (b) the killer must demonstrate non-identifiability holds under EVERY plausible estimator and measurement protocol, not just the one they chose to attack. When in doubt, the implementation is killed; the scientific question stays open until either (a) a survivor is found or (b) an explicit non-identifiability counterexample is constructed (two physically distinct latent states producing indistinguishable observations under ALL measurement protocols).', 'action_required': 'Explicit justification required to proceed despite this constraint'}, {'cemetery_entry': 'CE-018', 'territory': 'Cross-cutting (extracted from Round 62 capability collision failure; applies to ALL novelty claims)', 'mechanism': 'Capability collision test — keyword collision search is insufficient to establish novelty', 'epistemic_class': 'STRONG_CONSTRAINT', 'lesson': "FROZEN THEOREM CE-018: A novelty claim survives only when the candidate's CAPABILITY (what it can DO) is demonstrably absent from the prior art landscape — not when the candidate's KEYWORDS (what words it uses) are absent. The correct procedure: (1) decompose the candidate into its functional capabilities (e.g., 'intrapprocedural clot sensing' not 'retrieved-clot physical signature measurement'); (2) search the prior art landscape for each capability using the prior art's own vocabulary (assignee names, CPC classes, commercial product names, inventor terminology); (3) build a capability collision matrix mapping each capability to prior art coverage; (4) only if at least one capability is genuinely UNOCCUPIED (confirmed by both patent search AND commercial frontier analysis) can a novelty claim be recorded. Semantic re-skins (CE-012 violation) include: 'retrieved-clot' vs 'in-situ clot'; 'physical signature' vs 'composition'; 'integrated sensor' vs 'catheter-mounted sensor.' These distinctions prove nothing. The test is capability, not vocabulary.

SHARPENED (per CEO Round 62 audit): Capability novelty must be evaluated at the FUNCTIONAL END-TO-END level: input → inference → decision → physical effect → measurable outcome. Otherwise the machine can still find a 'novel' intermediate layer (e.g., a new sensor modality, a new feature, a new algorithm) that is already covered by an existing end-to-end system. The correct end-to-end test: (5) decompose the candidate into the complete causal loop — what is observed → what is inferred → what is predicted → what physical action becomes possible → what measurable outcome changes; (6) map each step of this loop to the prior art's end-to-end systems (not just individual capabilities); (7) only if the candidate's complete causal loop is demonstrably absent from the prior art's end-to-end systems can a novelty claim be recorded. A 'novel' intermediate layer that plugs into an existing end-to-end system is NOT novel — it is a substitution, not an invention. The unit of novelty is the complete causal loop, not the sensor, feature, algorithm, or capability.", 'action_required': 'Explicit justification required to proceed despite this constraint'}], 'informational': [{'cemetery_entry': 'CE-002', 'territory': 'CV-T02', 'mechanism': 'Multi-mechanism retention (size-selective + hydrodynamic)', 'epistemic_class': 'FAILURE_LESSON', 'lesson': "Always compare against the BEST SINGLE mechanism per payload class. A combined mechanism must DOMINATE all singles, not just be 'different'."}, {'cemetery_entry': 'CE-004', 'territory': 'CV-T04', 'mechanism': 'Derivative and predictive controllers for venous-aware regulation', 'epistemic_class': 'FAILURE_LESSON', 'lesson': "Derivative-based controllers are too sensitive to noise. Predictive models require accurate forward models that don't exist for CSF dynamics."}, {'cemetery_entry': 'CE-005', 'territory': 'CV-T05', 'mechanism': 'FDVBZ flow-diverting anti-fouling', 'epistemic_class': 'FAILURE_LESSON', 'lesson': 'Any anti-fouling mechanism that relies on flow direction must be tested against RETROGRADE flow. Retrograde flow is a realistic clinical scenario (cough, Valsalva, venous pressure changes).'}, {'cemetery_entry': 'CE-006', 'territory': 'CV-T06', 'mechanism': 'M3_REFINED electrothermal SMA retrieval', 'epistemic_class': 'FAILURE_LESSON', 'lesson': 'ALWAYS report worst-case reliability for clinical devices. Averages mask catastrophic failure modes. Thermal activation in a 37°C body environment has a narrow window (37-45°C = 8°C max). Sensor electronics are a SPOF that cannot be fully resolved by redundancy (common-mode failures).'}, {'cemetery_entry': 'CE-008', 'territory': 'CV-T08', 'mechanism': 'M5_REFINED adaptive over-drainage controller (sleep-state + venous pressure)', 'epistemic_class': 'UNRESOLVED_WARNING', 'lesson': "Do not assume VP shunt problems apply to the eShunt. The eShunt's drainage geometry is fundamentally different (short path, no siphon). Always verify the problem exists for the SPECIFIC device geometry. Over-drainage is siphon-driven; without a hydrostatic column, it may not occur."}, {'cemetery_entry': 'CE-010', 'territory': 'CV-T06', 'mechanism': 'Flow reversal obstruction clearing (R3)', 'epistemic_class': 'MODEL_DERIVED', 'lesson': 'Retrograde flush for eShunt pushes debris toward brain. The eShunt venous drainage direction makes retrograde more dangerous than VP shunts (peritoneal). However, the clinical hazard is ANALOGICAL (SAH blood causes inflammation), not directly proven for shunt debris. MODEL_DERIVED + ANALOGICAL_EVIDENCE — not PROVEN_UNSAFE.'}, {'cemetery_entry': 'CE-015', 'territory': 'RES-4 adaptive VSS (Round 56q-56t)', 'mechanism': 'RES-4 narrow: adaptive transverse/sigmoid sinus stent for CSF absorption regulation via AG pressure gradient control', 'epistemic_class': 'MODEL_BOUNDED_NEGATIVE_RESULT', 'lesson': 'MODEL-BOUNDED NEGATIVE RESULT: Before inventing variable geometry, calculate absolute pressure-control authority at the actual operating point. Relative r^4 sensitivity is meaningless if the absolute pressure drop is tiny. Under realistic post-stenting conditions (D=5-10mm, Q=200-500 mL/min), adaptive diameter control of a venous sinus produces <0.2 mmHg change in AG gradient — 5x below the 1 mmHg pre-registered threshold. Control authority exists only in the stenotic+high-flow regime (D≤4mm, Q≥1200 mL/min), which is incompatible with a stented patient whose stent has normalized diameter to 7-10mm. The network model (1323 configs) confirms: flow redistribution through contralateral sinus does NOT rescue control authority (dominance has no effect). NOT a universal vascular invariant — based on Poiseuille model with specific assumptions about geometry, flow, and topology.'}, {'cemetery_entry': 'CE-019', 'territory': 'CV-COMMERCIAL', 'mechanism': 'Minimum Sufficient Validation Evidence Derivation (MSVED) — 4-link chain: ML change → clinical pathway → risk envelope → minimum sufficient evidence → sufficiency proof', 'epistemic_class': 'VALIDATED_NEGATIVE', 'lesson': 'FROZEN THEOREM CE-019: A clinical-pathway-aware evidence selector must demonstrate that the clinical-pathway bridge produces a MATERIALLY DIFFERENT and BETTER evidence set than information-maximizing selection (BOED). If the pathway-aware selector uses MORE tests while achieving WORSE assurance, the clinical-pathway bridge adds complexity without value. The minimum-evidence claim must be validated by showing tests_required < BOED, not just tests_required < conventional. The killer experiment must compare against the STRONGEST available baseline (BOED), not just conventional full-validation.'}, {'cemetery_entry': 'CE-020', 'territory': 'CV-COMMERCIAL', 'mechanism': 'Automated Sufficiency Proof Generator (CC-04 / MSES theorem) — formal proof that a specific evidence set E is sufficient to establish modification-specific clinical risk envelope R(Δ)', 'epistemic_class': 'VALIDATED_NEGATIVE', 'lesson': 'FROZEN THEOREM CE-020: A sufficiency proof that is merely an integration of known statistical methods (NI testing + coverage + multiple-testing correction + sensitivity analysis) is NOT a novel mathematical result. Under §103, combining known methods to solve a problem the market explicitly asks for is likely obvious (KSR v. Teleflex). The frontier is a NEW MATHEMATICAL BOUND — e.g., a tight bound on minimum evidence set size that is better than what existing methods give individually, or a proof technique that connects clinical pathway coverage to statistical sufficiency in a way that is not derivable from existing theory. Additionally: killer tests for sufficiency proofs must include a TRUE POSITIVE case (sufficient evidence for a SAFE modification that the system correctly accepts), not just a true negative (insufficient evidence that the system correctly rejects).'}, {'cemetery_entry': 'CE-021', 'territory': 'CV-COMMERCIAL', 'mechanism': 'Non-Inferiority Statistical Engine (CC-08) — automated paired NI comparison with pre-registered margins for ML model modifications', 'epistemic_class': 'VALIDATED_NEGATIVE', 'lesson': 'FROZEN THEOREM CE-021: Automating a standard statistical test (NI testing) for a regulatory context that explicitly requires it (PCCP) is NOT an invention. Under KSR, combining known methods to solve a problem the market explicitly asks for is obvious. The coder correctly identified this in the R254 ranking ("NI testing is standard, high collision risk") but incorrectly chose to proceed. The CEO corrected: high collision risk is a RED FLAG, not a reason to proceed. Kill immediately if the smallest surviving mechanism is standard statistics + ML context + automated reporting.'}, {'cemetery_entry': 'CE-022', 'territory': 'CV-COMMERCIAL', 'mechanism': 'SGET (Strain-Gated Electrochemical Transduction) — A=strain pulse changes B=electrochemical sensor from 2D surface to 3D depth profiling. First synergy-2 candidate.', 'epistemic_class': 'VALIDATED_NEGATIVE — synergy without novelty', 'lesson': 'FROZEN THEOREM CE-022: Synergy ≠ novelty and synergy ≠ commercial moat. A functional interaction (A changes B) is NECESSARY but NOT SUFFICIENT for invention. The interaction itself — the causal law, the emergent effect, and functional equivalents across domains — must survive prior art independently. Additionally: synergy claims without quantitative comparison against the STRONGEST baseline are stories, not evidence. The unexpected-effect proof requires: (1) pre-registered quantitative prediction, (2) strongest baseline identified, (3) killer experiment vs that baseline, (4) result not predictable from A and B independently. The new standard: A changes B → unexpected effect → interaction survives prior art → reproducible advantage → cannot be cheaply reproduced → buyer value.'}, {'cemetery_entry': 'CE-023', 'territory': 'CV-SHUNT', 'mechanism': 'SC-05 Biofilm-Resistant Living-Surface Venous Interface — continuously renewing anti-biofilm surface with active surface-energy control at CSF-blood interface', 'epistemic_class': 'VALIDATED_NEGATIVE — concept not mechanism', 'lesson': 'FROZEN THEOREM CE-023: A candidate that survives the 14-gate protocol at the CONCEPT level can be killed at the ELEMENT-DECOMPOSITION level. The 14 gates assessed M4 against the broad concept (continuously renewing anti-biofilm surface) and found M4=NOT FOUND. But deep collision revealed that each element (continuous renewal, dynamic topography, surface-energy modulation) is individually occupied by prior art. The combination is an aggregation of known anti-fouling approaches. The lesson: M4 must be assessed at the ELEMENT level, not the concept level. And M4=NOT FOUND means the search has not found comparable performance yet — not that it does not exist.'}, {'cemetery_entry': 'CE-804', 'territory': 'L8-05', 'mechanism': 'unresolved for spinal fusion interbody cage', 'epistemic_class': 'FAILURE_LESSON', 'lesson': 'Do not pursue invention work in this territory until failure documentation exists'}, {'cem